# Rank 1028 / CVE-2022-30953 (SECURITY-2502): Blue Ocean's SCM endpoints let an
# attacker make Jenkins connect to a server of their choosing. getState() on the
# Github, Bitbucket and Git SCM classes validated a caller-supplied endpoint and
# reached out to it with no permission check, and the state was reachable by GET.
# The fixed revision adds a shared checkPermission() on AbstractScm requiring
# Item.CREATE on the root org folder, calls it from each getState(), enforces the
# POST method at runtime, and moves validateAndCreate from @PUT to @POST.
#
# ATTENTION, precision cost, third measurement of the same shape. Nothing focused
# fires either side of the pair: the whole tree reports the same twelve
# source/sink endpoints on the three SCM files in the vulnerable and the fixed
# revision (line numbers shift only), no rule row and no review flag names any
# getState. On the fixed tree the scanner marks the remediation itself —
# core.AuthorizationCheck flags on the new checkPermission calls in all three
# classes, none on the vulnerable tree — so the control vocabulary exists and the
# missing half is the issue side.
#
# The later-shipped Jenkins vocabulary does not reach here:
# JenkinsCredentialEndpointMissingPostPermission (VYQL-AUTH-073),
# JenkinsStaplerStateChangeMissingPost and JenkinsBuildScheduleMissingPermission
# all key on do*-prefixed descriptor method names, and getState is a REST
# resource method, not a Stapler form method. The remote half of the weakness
# dies behind interface-typed dispatch: validateExistingCredential(apiUrl) goes
# validateCredential -> getApi -> BitbucketApiFactory.resolve(...).create(...) ->
# api.getUser(), the receiver stays at the BitbucketApi interface type, no
# UrlFetch label exists in the module, and trace stops at the cross-package
# boundary — the interface-dispatch gap already recorded against rank 1339.
#
# The two rules this CVE invites are the ones measured and rejected.
# Requiring a permission check on REST endpoints: the plugin has 46 endpoint
# methods in its main sources while only 16 files call hasPermission or
# checkPermission at all, and three endpoints needed the fix, so the rule reports
# on the order of thirty sites for three true positives. Requiring a particular
# HTTP verb annotation was measured at rank 1027 on jenkinsci/bitbucket-branch-
# source-plugin, where 19 doFill/doCheck/doTest methods carried exactly one
# annotation between them even after that plugin's own security fix. The
# authorization variant was measured at rank 1011 on getarcaneapp/arcane at 4.1
# per cent package-scoped and 19.5 per cent file-scoped. Three independent
# codebases give the same answer: endpoints legitimately differ in whether they
# need a guard and the structure does not say which. A narrower binding keying on
# getState or validateExistingAccessToken names this project's own layout, not
# any library's documented API, so the next variant of the weakness walks past it.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-precision-cost

test "rank1028: SCM state endpoint validates a caller endpoint with no permission check"
  lang java
  file blueocean-github-pipeline/src/main/java/io/jenkins/blueocean/blueocean_github_pipeline/GithubScm.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-073
  code
  ```
  public class GithubScm extends AbstractScm {
      @Override
      public Object getState() {
          this.validateExistingAccessToken();
          return super.getState();
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1028: bitbucket state endpoint reads the caller apiUrl and validates a credential against it"
  lang java
  file blueocean-bitbucket-pipeline/src/main/java/io/jenkins/blueocean/blueocean_bitbucket_pipeline/AbstractBitbucketScm.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-073
  code
  ```
  public abstract class AbstractBitbucketScm extends AbstractScm {
      @Override
      public Object getState() {
          StaplerRequest request = Stapler.getCurrentRequest();
          Objects.requireNonNull(request, "Must be called in HTTP request context");

          String apiUrl = request.getParameter("apiUrl");

          ErrorMessage message = new ErrorMessage(400, "Invalid request");
          if(StringUtils.isBlank(apiUrl)) {
              message.add(new ErrorMessage.Error("apiUrl", ErrorMessage.Error.ErrorCodes.MISSING.toString(),
                  "apiUrl is required parameter"));
          }
          try {
              new URL(apiUrl);
          } catch (MalformedURLException e) {
              message.add(new ErrorMessage.Error("apiUrl", ErrorMessage.Error.ErrorCodes.INVALID.toString(),
                  "apiUrl parameter must be a valid URL"));
          }
          if(!message.getErrors().isEmpty()){
              throw new ServiceException.BadRequestException(message);
          }
          validateExistingCredential(apiUrl);
          return super.getState();
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1028: fix requires Item.CREATE before returning the state"
  lang java
  file blueocean-github-pipeline/src/main/java/io/jenkins/blueocean/blueocean_github_pipeline/GithubScm.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-073
  code
  ```
  public class GithubScm extends AbstractScm {
      @Override
      public Object getState() {
          checkPermission();
          this.validateExistingAccessToken();
          return super.getState();
      }

      protected void checkPermission() {
          AccessControlled rootOrgFolder = getRootOrgFolder();
          if (!rootOrgFolder.hasPermission(Item.CREATE)) {
              throw new ServiceException.ForbiddenException("You do not have Job/Create permission");
          }
      }
  }
  ```
